<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bertrand d'Ogeron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1613–1676</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bertrand d'Ogeron was a French colonial governor appointed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-west-india-company">French West India Company</a> in 1665 to govern Tortuga and the French settlements on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>. He encouraged buccaneers to settle as planters, brought settlers and women from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and organised the colony that became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a>, later France's richest colony. He served until 1675.</p></div>
